.Dd October 13, 2026
.Dt GIT-GUD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm git-gud
.Nd manage git-gud repository hooks
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm install
.Op Fl f | Fl -force
.Op Ar directory
.Nm
.Cm version
.Op Ar directory
.Nm
.Cm run
.Ar hook
.Op Ar hook-arguments ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
installs and runs git lua hooks for repository automation.
.Pp
The installed hooks load a Lua configuration file and run registered handlers for
Git events.
By default the configuration is read from
.Pa ~/.config/git/gud.lua
when it exists, otherwise
.Pa ~/.config/git-gud/init.lua .
Set
.Ev GIT_GUD_INIT
to use a different configuration file.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width install
.It Cm install Op Fl f | Fl -force Op Ar directory
Install
.Nm
into the specified hooks directory and link supported hook names to it.
If no directory is specified, use the current repository's hooks directory.
The specified directory must already exist; it does not need to belong to a Git repository.
Refuses to overwrite an existing installation unless
.Fl f
or
.Fl -force
is supplied.
.It Cm version Op Ar directory
Print the command version and the version installed in the specified directory,
if present.
If no directory is specified, check the current repository's hooks directory.
.It Cm run Ar hook Op Ar hook-arguments ...
Run a supported hook directly in the current repository, without installing it.
Pass the same arguments Git would pass to that hook:
.Cm commit-msg
requires a commit message file path;
.Cm post-checkout
requires the previous ref, new ref, and checkout flag (0 for a file checkout, 1 for a branch checkout).
.El
.Sh HOOKS
The supported hooks are:
.Bl -tag -width post-checkout
.It Cm post-checkout
Runs after a checkout and invokes registered Lua checkout handlers.
.It Cm commit-msg
Runs before a commit is created and invokes registered Lua commit-message handlers, passing in the commit message info
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width GIT_GUD_TRACE_SYSLOG
.It Ev GIT_GUD_INIT
Path to the Lua configuration file. Defaults to
.Pa ~/.config/git/gud.lua
when it exists, otherwise
.Pa ~/.config/git-gud/init.lua .
.It Ev GIT_GUD_TRACE_SYSLOG
Enable syslog logging for
.Nm
and its hooks, and set its verbosity.
When unset, no syslog messages are sent.
Set to
.Cm DEBUG
to include debug messages,
.Cm WARN
or
.Cm WARNING
to include warnings and more severe messages, or any other value to include
informational and more severe messages.
Messages use the
.Nm
syslog identity.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr git 1 ,
.Xr githooks 5
